    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "907ac6a8_ec18812a",
        "filename": "board/ryu_sh/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 60,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-16T16:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Beyond these two fields, motion_sensor_t also has fields for the run-time values of odr and range (which appear to only be used during init). I think that perhaps those fields should be removed in order to deduplicate. Let the driver keep track of the current state, and have the motion sensor get/set on demand.\n\nIt *could* be more generic, if we were to also include resolution. The kxcj9 has a configurable resolution so it\u0027s included in its driver data structure. However, the lsm6ds0 has a fixed resolution so that is why I did not include it in the lsm6ds0_data structure. It would be wasting a field of every instance of it.\n\n\nPlus this way, if we were to add a different sensor, the driver private data structure would only have to be as big as the run-time configurable parameters.",
      "parentUuid": "904c868c_38e471d5",
      "revId": "50fd9bb8e312c3afc5dfd2f08262199e8a58e1b3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
